item.description:
arXiv:2412.16890v4 Announce Type: replace 
Abstract: In this paper, we first establish the quantitative properties for positive solutions to the Moser-Trudinger equation in the two-dimensional Poincar\'e disk $\mathbb{B}^2$: \begin{equation*}\label{mt1}
  \left\{
  \begin{aligned}
  &-\Delta_{\mathbb{B}^2}u=\lambda ue^{u^2},\ x\in\mathbb{B}^2,
  &u\to0,\ \text{when}\ \rho(x)\to\infty,
  &\|\nabla_{\mathbb{B}^2} u\|_{L^2(\mathbb{B}^2)}^2\leq M_0,
  \end{aligned}
  \right. \end{equation*} where $0<\lambda<\frac{1}{4}=\inf\limits_{u\in W^{1,2}(\mathbb{B}^2)\backslash\{0\}}\frac{\|\nabla_{\mathbb{B}^2}u\|_{L^2(\mathbb{B}^2)}^2}{\|u\|_{L^2(\mathbb{B}^2)}^2}$, $\rho(x)$ denotes the geodesic distance between $x$ and the origin and $M_0$ is a fixed large positive constant (see Theorem \ref{thm1}). Furthermore, by carefully analyzing the asymptotic expansion of the Dirichlet energy \(\|\nabla_{\mathbb{B}^2} u\|_{L^2(\mathbb{B}^2)}^2\) as \(\lambda \to 0\), and establishing that \[ \lim_{\substack{\lambda \to 1/4}} \int_{\mathbb{B}^2} |\nabla_{\mathbb{B}^2} u_\lambda|^2 \, dV_{\mathbb{B}^2} = +\infty \] for~the ~nonzero~least energy solution, we are able to prove the existence of a critical point for the Moser-Trudinger functional \(F(u) = \int_{\mathbb{B}^2} (e^{u^2} - 1) \, dV_{\mathbb{B}^2}\) under the constraint \(\int_{\mathbb{B}^2} |\nabla_{\mathbb{B}^2} u|^2 \, dV_{\mathbb{B}^2} = \Lambda\) for \(\Lambda \in (4\pi, +\infty)\), up to some M\"{o}bius transformation. This result is substantially different from the non-existence of critical points for the Moser-Trudinger functional in the Euclidean disk.
  Finally, by applying a local Pohozaev identity around the origin and exploiting the uniqueness of solutions to the Cauchy initial value problem for ODEs, we prove that the Moser-Trudinger equation has a unique positive solution up to some M\"{o}bius transformation when $\lambda$ is close to $0$.
